XSA_PLAN v=6 pipeline=v2bin (bin shape: one sweep -> 256 byte-bins -> ordered stitch -> decomposed fused finish; no chunk phase, no merge walk) corpus_bytes=1115411 chunks=1 kway=1 threads=1 cap_gb=2 cores=256 cx16=true mem_available_gb=805
XSA_PLAN_PHASES name wall disc_peak_gb rss_gb
XSA_PLAN_PHASE name=bin(sweep) wall=0:00:00 wall_s=0 disc_peak_gb=0.0 rss_gb=0.02
XSA_PLAN_PHASE name=bin(build) wall=0:00:00 wall_s=0 disc_peak_gb=0.0 rss_gb=0.02
XSA_PLAN_PHASE name=bin(stitch) wall=0:00:00 wall_s=0 disc_peak_gb=0.1 rss_gb=0.02
XSA_PLAN_PHASE name=fused-finish wall=0:00:00 wall_s=0 disc_peak_gb=0.0 rss_gb=0.00
XSA_PLAN_TOTAL wall=0:00:00 wall_s=0 (TERM SUM)
XSA_PLAN_TOTAL_NOTE the sum above is the TERM SUM; the bin producer and the fused finish overlap, so the wall is max(producer, finish) = XSA_PLAN_V2_BIN_END e2e
XSA_PLAN_V2_TERMS pipeline=v2bin corpus_gb=0.0 rlebwt_gb=0.0 pfck2_scratch_gb=0.0 pieces_window_gb=0.0 container_gb=0.0 tree_peak_gb=0.0 whole_box_gb=0.0
XSA_PLAN_V2_TREE tree_peak=1.975n bound=2.5n measured_at=1GB-G2 (output side; the bin producer's own addition is the rolling window files, priced above); whole_box(corpus+tree)=2.975n; position column disc=0.000n (transient rolling window files only)
XSA_PLAN_V2_WITNESS witness stream = 8B x chi; chi/n = 0.283 is the 1GB FIXTURE ratio (the pile value is unmeasured): ~0 GB at this scale; if it exceeds --wit-ram-budget the overflow spills as sorted varint-delta disc runs (est. <= 0.3x raw, EXTRAPOLATED - unmeasured at spill scale) inside the tree
XSA_PLAN_V2_TRANSIENT no chunk set, no merge transient, no persistent position column: the producer's scratch is the piece window (0.033 GiB, W=1100 bands x 65536 runs), the rlebwt it is publishing (0.0 GiB) and the ROLLING WINDOW FILES (0.0 GiB on disc = 2 credit x cap x 8 B, one file per live window, unlinked the moment its bins are built); the build's RAM is one group (0.0 GiB, 16 B/slot) and NEVER the window; inputs the finish consumes are unlinked as read; witness spill reserve 0.0 GiB (0.3x overflow, EXTRAPOLATED)
XSA_PLAN_V2_CAP live_cap_slots=1115411 source=auto from --memory-gb 2 (bound by address space) bound_by=address space (--memory-gb): corpus cache + fill staging + 16 B/slot arena pair; MEMORY bound: 90% of --memory-gb 2 GiB (2147483648 B) = 1932735283 B usable - corpus cache 1115411 B (min(n, 512 B x pool slots 1048576)) - staging 41943040 B (1 threads x (33554432 B fill + 8388608 B leaf)) = 1889676832 B / 16 B per build-group slot = 118104802 slots; SCRATCH bound: 90% of 483.7 GiB free = 467465468313 B - rlebwt+pieces 37417577 B = 467428050736 B / (credit 2 x 8 B per slot) = 1115411 slots; window_file_gb=0.02 = credit x cap x 8 B ON DISC (0 B of address space: the fill writes with buffered pwrite, never a mapping); the finish is its own process under the same cap: witness 0.0 GiB fits it, headroom_pct=90
XSA_PLAN_V2_RAMSPLIT pool_gb=0.50 pool_share_of_memory_pct=25.0 pool_covers_corpus_pct=100.0 fill_stage_gb=0.03 leaf_stage_gb=0.01 arena_group_gb=1.76 finish_witness_gb=0.00 finish_pfck_grid_gb=0.00 usable_gb=1.80 rule=the pool is sized FIRST and pinned to the whole corpus text whenever --memory-gb allows (the hot set is the boilerplate epoch); the two staging buffers are constants per thread; the arena pair takes the remainder; the finish is a second process under the same cap and owns its witness stream + pfck grid
XSA_PLAN_V2_BIN live_cap_slots=1115411 windows=1 window_file_gb=0.0 ram_group_gb=0.0 count_s=0 fill_s=0 build_s=0 stitch_s=0 producer_s=0 finish_s=0
XSA_PLAN_V2_TARGET rows=262144 leaves=5 levels_per_row=3.49 largest_leaf_rows<=262144 rule=subdivide-while-rows>target (depth is an OUTPUT of the census; the depth cap is a fail-loud backstop, not the rule)
XSA_PLAN_V2_POSITION_STORE window_file_gb=0.02 = credit(2) x cap(1115411) x 8 B ON DISC (one rolling file per live window, unlinked when built); ram_group_gb=0.02 = 16 B/slot x the group being sorted in place; position_io_gb=0.0 = 16 x n / (8+8) B a position written once and read once; position_io_s=0 at the 5.238 GB/s device floor (overlapped by the fill and the build, so not on the critical path); persistent_position_column=0 full_SA=0
XSA_PLAN_V2_BIN_END e2e_s=0 e2e=0:00:00 producer=0:00:00 finish=0:00:00 rule=max(producer,finish) (concurrent, flow-controlled through the piece window)
XSA_PLAN_V2_BIN_NOTE 1 windows = ceil(n/1115411) (each window re-reads the whole corpus: fill = windows x n at the 5.238 GB/s device floor = 0.00 h at this scale); bins are indivisible so a window is packed to <= cap by whole bins (every measured point matches ceil exactly: 1 GB cap 250M -> 5, 1 GB cap>=n -> 1); a single bin larger than the cap makes the producer raise it (BIN_CAP_RAISED) and the front door FAILS LOUD rather than price a different arena. The TREE: 5 leaves = ceil(n/target), each a comparison sort of <= 262144 rows (depth is an OUTPUT of the byte census; mean levels/row 3.49 measured at this target, i.e. the emergent depth is 0 for the busiest bucket, not a parameter). Terms (s/GB at 1 GB): count 1.360 fill 0.191+0.191/window build 107.930@1t stitch 11.408 = producer 120.89; finish 118.90 (own work); e2e = max = 120.89. Measured 1 GB producer wall 41.68 s and with-finish 142.18 s (flow-limited): the model holds the producer term to 290.0%
XSA_PLAN_TAPE envelope_gb=1.00 memory_gb=2 bytes_per_row=90 bands_in_flight=1 rows_per_band=66227 rows_per_band_budget=9224690 binding=scratch-window bands=1 waves=17 rows_per_wave=66227 arena_gb=0.77 fixed_gb=0.03 stage_gb=0.06 peak_gb=0.86 peak_ratio_pct=86 bound=90 arena_planned_gb=0.01 headroom_pct=85 rule=rows_per_band=(envelope-fixed-stage)x85%/(bytes_per_row x bands_in_flight) n_is_in_no_numerator=1 n=1115412
XSA_PLAN_V2_HOSTING all-phase scratch peak 0.1 GiB = 49.546n on one host; free 483.7 GiB: FITS (corpus itself excluded; add 0.0 GiB if co-hosted)
XSA_PLAN_DISC FEASIBLE: ALL-PHASE peak 0.1 GiB vs 483.7 GiB free (bin shape: rolling window FILES + rlebwt + piece window + container; the build's RAM is one group, never the window)
XSA_PLAN_RAM FEASIBLE: the band arena is 0.8 GiB = 1 bands in flight x 66227 rows x 90 B/row + 0.0 GiB fixed + 0.1 GiB staging = 0.86 GiB, 86% of the 1.00 GiB envelope (--memory-gb 2, the bound is 90%); 1 bands per wave, 17 waves; the producer asserts the same ratio at exit (SS_TAPE_PEAK) and the front door refuses the run if the two plans disagree
